<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Android Auto Backup rules for API 26-30 (see data_extraction_rules.xml for 31+).

    The Room database is excluded so the backend remains the only thing that
    restores workout data (ADR-0017).

    This is not a size or privacy precaution. Auto Backup silently reinstates the
    app's previous database when the app is installed, which made the database
    non-empty before the app had run a line of code, so restore correctly decided
    there was nothing to do and declined. The result was a device showing its old
    local state while the backend held strictly more: verified on the physical
    OnePlus on 2026-08-07, where the phone came back with one routine and no
    history while the backend had two routines and two completed workouts.

    Two mechanisms racing to restore the same rows is worse than either alone, and
    the backend is the one that is authoritative, nightly-backed-up, and shared
    across devices. Auto Backup's copy is a silent, stale, single-device snapshot
    whose rows are already marked SYNCED, so nothing would ever reconcile them.

    Everything else still backs up, including the settings DataStore.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="database" path="myfitnesslog.db" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="myfitnesslog.db-wal" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="myfitnesslog.db-shm" />
</full-backup-content>
